      <div type="clause" n="6">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 6</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>Be wiccecræftum. Ond we cwædon be þam wiccecræftum ⁊ be liblacum ⁊ be morðdædum, gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.7"/> þær<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.4"/> acweald wære, ⁊ he his ætsacan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.star3"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.16"/> ne mihte, þæt he beo his feores<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.17"/> scyldig.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>[Be<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.24"/> wiccecræftum.] And we cwedon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.29"/> be ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.3"/> wiccecræftum ⁊ be lyblacu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ⁊ morðdædu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.1"/> ðær man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.30"/> acweald wære, ⁊ he his<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.31"/> ætsacan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.star"/> ne mæge, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he beo his feores scyldig.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-so"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>Be wiccecræftum ⁊ liblacum. We cwædon be þam wiccecræftum ⁊ liblacum ⁊ morðdædum, gif þær mon acweald wære, ⁊ he his oðsacan ne mæg, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he beo his feores scyldig.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.16-2"/><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>De sortilegis et liblacis.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.28"/> Decreuimus etiam de sortilegis et liblacis et mortem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.29-2"/> dantibus, si hominem occidant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.30-2"/> et negare non possint, uitę<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.31-2"/> suę culpa iudicetur.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.oe.32"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="6" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="130" ed="#attenborough"/>Be wiccecræftum. Ond we cwædon be þam wiccecræftum ⁊ be liblacum ⁊ be morðdædum, gif mon þær acweald<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IIAs_6.attnote.fn.12"/> wære, ⁊ he his ætsacan<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_6.attnote.fn.8"/><ptr type="editorNote" n="*" target="#IIAs_6.attnote.fn.star"/> ne mihte<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_6.attnote.fn.13"/>, þæt he beo his feores scyldig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>Von Zauberkünsten (und Verhexungen. <hi rend="italic">So</hi>). Und wir bestimmten über die Zauberkünste und über Verhexungen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.de.1"/> und über verstohlene Lebensgefährdungen, wenn ein Mensch dadurch getödtet wird, und der [Verklagte] es [überhaupt] nicht leugnen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.de.2"/> kann, dass er sein Leben verwirkt habe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_6.lnote.de.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of witchcraft (and sorcery. So). And we determined concerning witchcraft and sorcery and secret attempts on life, if a person is killed by them and the [accused] cannot deny it [at all], that he shall have forfeited his life.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="131" ed="#attenborough"/>And we have declared with regard to witchcrafts and sorceries and deadly spells<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_6.attnote.n.1"/>, if death is occasioned thereby, and [the accused] cannot deny it [the charge], that he shall forfeit his life.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="419" ed="#whitelock"/>Concerning witchcrafts. And we have pronounced concerning witchcrafts and sorceries and secret attempts on life,<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_6.whinote.n.4"/> that, if anyone is killed by such, and he [the accused] cannot deny it, he is to forfeit his life.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="153"><ref target="clause:EGu_11">EGu 11</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. EGu. 11</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Blas_1">Blas 1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="367"><ref target="clause:Blas_Inscr">Blas</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">B breaks off after ‘ætsacan’ at the end of a quire (the following leaves are lost; Af 3 follows in B); Liebermann continues with Ld. Liebermann compares EGu 11.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Ld; Raum für Rubrik B</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so Ld; space for a rubric B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cwædon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cwædon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mon acwealde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mon acwealde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hit <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hit Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">endet eine Lage; folgen sollende Blätter fehlen; folgt</hi> Af 3 [<hi rend="italic">o. S.</hi> 51] <hi rend="italic">B.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a gathering ends; the leaves that should follow are missing; there follows Af 3 [above p. 51] B.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oðsacan <hi rend="italic">in So originaler</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oðsacan more original in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æt <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æt on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.16-2" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Raum für Rubriken Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">space for rubrics Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">maleficis <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> et mortem dantibus <hi rend="italic">fügt zu MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">maleficis T; et mortem dantibus added by MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.29-2" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sortem <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sortem Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.30-2" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-derint <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-derint TMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.31-2" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wite <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wite T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-centur <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-centur TMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q wusste die Bed. nicht, auch I Em 6. <hi rend="italic">Lybb:</hi> ‘Gesundheit affizierender Trank’; <hi rend="italic">unlybban</hi> synonym mit <hi rend="italic">attor</hi> braucht Ælfric <hi rend="italic">Hom.</hi> II 158. ‘Gift’ (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3; Zauber 2. 3) ist hier mitgemeint</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q did not know the meaning, in I Em 6 either. <hi rend="italic">Lybb:</hi> ‘potion affecting health’; Ælfric <hi rend="italic">Hom.</hi> II 158 uses <hi rend="italic">unlybban</hi> as synonymous with <hi rend="italic">attor</hi>. ‘Poison’ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3; Zauber 2. 3) is included in the meaning here</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> 4²</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 4²</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_6.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Mord 7—8; Todesstrafe 3 g</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Mord 7—8; Todesstrafe 3 g</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_6.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">See E. and G. cap. 11, note.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_6.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>ætsacan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">oðsacan</hi>. So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_6.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>acweald</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mon acwealde</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
